  458/460 149th Pennsylvania Infantry Monument       the report gives this regiment two dedications (1886; 1888, a larger monument, the old one moved to Hancock Avenue) and the site lists the regiment twice (entry 458, MN 31-C, on the First Day field; entry 460, MN 248, on Hancock Avenue). The report implies that the monument of 1888 stands where MN031-C is and the old one on Hancock Avenue, but no sentence says which of the two entries is which, so neither is given a year
  442/443 121st Pennsylvania Infantry Monument       the report gives this regiment two dedications (1886 obelisk; 1888 replacement, the old monument moved to Hancock Avenue) and the site lists the regiment twice (entry 442, MN 47-B, on the First Day field; entry 443, MN 246, on Hancock Avenue). The report implies that the replacement of 1888 stands where MN047-B is and the old one on Hancock Avenue, but no sentence says which of the two entries is which, so neither is given a year
      143 First Shot Marker (8th Illinois Cavalry)   the report's park number MN001 (Cavalry Monument Group, 8th Illinois, dedicated 1891) is the number the site gives to its First Shot Marker (entry 143); the site gives the 8th Illinois Cavalry Monument (entry 144) the number MN 39. The two lists disagree, so neither entry is matched
      492 2nd Wisconsin Infantry Monument            the report numbers the 2nd Wisconsin monument group MN034-D; the site gives its 2nd Wisconsin Infantry Monument (entry 492) the number MN 35-D. The two lists disagree, so it is not matched
